<article class="env-lemma" id="02WL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02WL">Lemma <span data-tag="02WL">65.5.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme contained in $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$. Let $F, G, H : (\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}^{opp} \to \textit{Sets}$. Let $\mathcal{P}$ be a property as in Definition <a href="/tag/025V" data-tag="025V">65.5.1</a>. Let $a : F \to G$ be a representable transformation of functors. Let $b : H \to G$ be any transformation of functors. Consider the fibre product diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ H \times _{b, G, a} F \ar[r]_-{b'} \ar[d]_{a'} &  F \ar[d]^ a \\  H \ar[r]^ b &  G }  \]
</div>
  <p> If $a$ has property $\mathcal{P}$ then also the base change $a'$ has property $\mathcal{P}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that the lemma makes sense by Lemma <a href="/tag/02WB" data-tag="02WB">65.3.3</a>. Proof omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>